## Disposition sufficiency (the UX bank point)

The UX spot check (ux-browser-review-p2-0aed743.json) failed on one point only: the bank
judge note misreads the chandelier shadows as floor wheels. The spot check itself records
zero impact: its own bank rating is 7.5 (the judge's is 7.5), all 8 sampled ratings stay
within 1.0, no bar outcome flips, and no critical is missed.

The orchestrator disposition (plan.md:66-75, commit 56bdd0cf) is sufficient for acceptance:

- The factual core is source-verified by this audit: scenes/maps/bank.ts line 4 places the
  three chandeliers at [-2,2,2.2], [3.5,2,0.5], [-3.5,2,-2], all at y=2. The judge note's
  "sit at floor level" is contradicted by the source alone.
- The judge files stay unchanged as true records of what the judge wrote. Rewriting them
  would falsify evidence. The correction lives in plan.md, the execution source of truth.
- The escalation path stays open: the plan header records that the PM may reverse each
  decision taken 2026-11-19.
- No phase outcome changes: bank stays above 7.0 either way and stays out of the Phase 3
  rework set; mill stays in the rework set either way (5.5, critical true).
- The mill disposition is verified too: assets/watermill.ts line 20 sets WCX = 1.15 and
  line 116 builds the radius-1.2 rim, so the wheel exists and Phase 3 fixes only the yaw or
  the shot angle. Phase 3 builds no new wheel.

